    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "you say a \"balanced approach\" is crucial, but that almost feels like a way to avoid the actual question. if we prioritize \"triumphs and shared values\" to avoid division, aren't we just glossing over the parts of history that students need to understand to be truly informed? isn't it more effective to teach them the hard truths about systemic injustices so they can actually learn from them? why is the \"triumphs\" side considered the better baseline here?",
